      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T22:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there some existing call to `usb_mux_set`, using `get_mux_mode_to_set` incorrectly, which is happening at the wrong time and should be removed?",
      "revId": "fee06cf333fa2c34fb8fd7f0cebd46e866161fed",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d62d763_a26ee147",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2520,
      "author": {
        "id": 1533827
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T01:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are other calls to `get_mux_mode_to_set` - through `set_usb_mux_with_current_data_role` - which clobber the desired mux connection.\n\nThe two functions that I see that are being called that does this are \n1. `tc_set_data_role` and \n2. `handle_new_power_state`.\nBut there are a total of 12 functions throughout that can call it.\n\nEither `set_usb_mux_with_current_data_role` must be replaced with a raw `mux_set` in these functions, or, probably more preferably, the `get_mux_mode_to_set` function must return a connected mux state regardless of where it\u0027s being called from.",
      "parentUuid": "7a8b7a70_e63bd822",
      "revId": "fee06cf333fa2c34fb8fd7f0cebd46e866161fed",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
